# (round 187, #203) `t[i]` on a tensor in a NUMERIC context reads the raw
# element: a matmul that overflowed to inf compares as inf, as the VM's flat
# buffer read does (boxing first clamped it to 1e308 -- test_store's
# divergence). Printing still boxes (both sides show 1e+308). A shaped buffer
# indexes flat; out of range is caught with the VM's kind.
nb is buffer of 4
nb[0] is 1e300
nb[1] is 1e300
nb[2] is 1e300
nb[3] is 1e300
nm is reshape of [nb, 2, 2]
np is matmul of [nm, nm]
print of (np[0] > 1e308)
print of np[0]
print of (np[3] > 1e308)
sb is buffer of 3
sb[0] is 1
sb[1] is 2
sb[2] is 3
sm is reshape of [sb, 3, 1]
sr is reshape of [sb, 1, 3]
sq is matmul of [sr, sm]
print of (sq[0] + 0.5)
print of (sq[0] * 2 == 28)
try:
    print of (sq[3] + 1)
catch e:
    print of e.kind
